{"name":"Tree Sap","hex":"#cc7711","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree sap","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fluid that circulates within the phloem of a tree to distribute water and nutrients."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree_sap"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sap","blocks":[{"text":"Sap is a fluid transported in the xylem cells or phloem sieve tube elements of a plant. These cells transport water and nutrients throughout the plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Sap_of_Sansevieria_trifasciata.jpg/330px-Sap_of_Sansevieria_trifasciata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sap"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Common_jassid_nymph_feeding.jpg/500px-Common_jassid_nymph_feeding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Common_jassid_nymph_feeding.jpg/1280px-Common_jassid_nymph_feeding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Common_jassid_nymph_feeding.jpg/500px-Common_jassid_nymph_fe